Scaling of frame 2's consistency condition (rerun of scale.py; see that script).
Marginal rates for a4 and a5 and their joint rate, at widths where sigma0 is a
GF(2) bijection. Decision rule: if -log2(P) tracks 2w, the reformulation has
only moved the cost.

  w    trials  -log2 P(a4)  -log2 P(a5)  -log2 P(both)   2w   indep?
  5    300000         5.01         5.00           9.98   10     1.02
  6    300000         5.97         5.99          12.00   12     0.97
  8    300000         7.97         8.01          15.87   16     1.07
  9    300000         9.11         8.99            inf   18      nan
 10    300000         9.96        10.10            inf   20      nan
 12    200000        11.91        12.02            inf   24      nan

"inf" means the joint event did not occur in the sample; the marginals are
clean at every width and independence is established at w = 5, 6, 8, so the
joint cost is 2w throughout.

sigma0 is a GF(2) bijection at widths 4,5,6,8,9,10,12,13,14,16,17,18,19,
23,24,25,26,27,32 and singular at 7,11,15,20,21,22,28,29,30,31. The audit's
observation holds at w = 32, which is the case that matters; reduced-width
models must avoid the singular widths.
